  "2026-09-02T11:39:03.677Z","harness:codex","Upstream dependency evidence: pm-changelog PR #174 merged at 7a643eb0, merged-main CI and CodeQL passed, and manual workflow_dispatch release 33624794970 published npm/GitHub tag v2026.9.2. Consuming that immutable release now to remove the UTC wall-clock changelog drift exposed by pm-cli Gates (static)."
  "2026-09-02T11:43:08.623Z","harness:codex","Temporary-directory acceptance: a fresh Git/npm project was initialized with the branch CLI, qa-context was created and closed, pm-changelog 2026.9.2 was installed through pm package install, and changelog generation under UTC, Europe/Vienna, and America/Los_Angeles produced byte-identical JSON. The untagged package version heading was 2099.1.2 with no fabricated date and contained qa-context. The first assertion expected Unreleased, which was stricter than the actual --release-version-from-package contract; the corrected contract assertion passed. Temporary data was removed."
  "2026-09-02T12:20:48.192Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review implementation: authoritative append state now survives projection-invalidation contention without retrying the immutable append; path-like stream IDs are rejected before indexed validation; signal snapshots reject blank or duplicate candidate IDs before serialization; SDK init preserves nonblank PM_PATH as an explicit tracker target; timestamp failures use the canonical history_timestamp_invalid envelope while lossless trailing-zero fractions remain accepted; owned lock release outlasts the stale-cleanup threshold and performs a final token ownership check; history override fixtures now contain all lock artifacts within their temporary tracker. Focused regression verification passed 7 files / 155 tests."
  "2026-09-02T12:38:18.597Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review correction evidence: authoritative history append now executes at most once when post-append index invalidation is contended; candidate snapshots reject blank or duplicate IDs before persistence and their digest is anchored against the production serializer; path-like stream IDs are rejected before indexed lookup without provoking rebuild; invalid history timestamp precision uses the stable history_timestamp_invalid taxonomy while accepting only zero-valued sub-millisecond tails; stale lock release waits through the full cleanup-gate lease and removes its lock only after ownership re-verification; SDK init honors explicit PM_PATH without changing active-host cwd discovery; history override tests keep lock artifacts inside their sandbox. Focused suites passed, TypeScript and ESLint passed, and the PM-linked repo-wide coverage gate passed at exactly 61,220/61,220 statements, 46,255/46,255 branches, 12,739/12,739 functions, and 58,924/58,924 lines."
  "2026-09-02T12:39:06.786Z","harness:codex","Static-gate note: the first post-review pnpm quality:static run passed ESLint, both zero-duplication checks, build, contract snapshots, and generated capability surfaces, then correctly failed because the new stable history_timestamp_invalid code made the generated error-code catalog stale. Refreshing that generated contract before rerunning the complete gate."
  "2026-09-02T12:39:57.010Z","harness:codex","Static-gate note: after refreshing the generated error-code catalog, the second complete run passed lint, duplication, and build, then correctly detected the corresponding full contract fixture drift. Refreshing the intentional generated contract snapshot before the final complete rerun."
  "2026-09-02T12:49:49.138Z","harness:codex","Final static evidence: after refreshing the generated error-code catalog and contract fixture and restoring runtime.ts to the repository's intentional compact public-surface layout, the complete CI-mode pnpm quality:static gate passed. It verified ESLint, zero duplicated chunks, build, generated contracts, 100% source/export/member docstrings, file/directory/complexity limits, package boundaries, SDK parity, replication, grammar, refusal closure, token budgets, MCP deprecation dispositions, context quality, graph composition, and record integrity."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T15:48:17.264Z","harness:codex","Freshness is semantic event provenance, not file-write time: maintenance operations must be explicitly classified and excluded from temporal ranking, while unknown operations fail closed as substantive."
  "2026-09-01T19:41:37.711Z","harness:codex","A derived index can safely coordinate an authoritative append without a second filesystem lock by holding its SQLite write transaction across the append and paired size capture; if projection work fails after the append, preserve authority and discard the accelerator."
  "2026-09-01T20:11:24.024Z","harness:codex","SQLite row transactions alone do not coordinate a replace-by-rename rebuild or a stat-then-query read. A derived index that must be linearizable with compliant authoritative appends needs one shared cross-process coordination boundary spanning rebuild, append, validation, and read; the SQLite transaction remains the inner atomic projection commit."
